  "content_blocks": [
    {
      "block_id": "b00000",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Procurements started before 24 February 2025",
      "ordinal": 0,
      "heading_path": [
        "Procurements started before 24 February 2025"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00001",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "The Public Contracts Regulations 2015 apply to procurements of goods, services or works commenced before 24 February 2025.",
      "ordinal": 1,
      "heading_path": [
        "Procurements started before 24 February 2025"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00002",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "The Utilities Contracts Regulations 2016 apply to utilities procurements commenced before 24 February 2025.",
      "ordinal": 2,
      "heading_path": [
        "Procurements started before 24 February 2025"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00003",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "The Concession Contracts Regulations 2016 apply to all in-scope concessions advertised in the FTS before 24 February 2025, whether by a contracting authority or by a utility. The CCR 2016 apply to over threshold public works concessions and public services concessions.",
      "ordinal": 3,
      "heading_path": [
        "Procurements started before 24 February 2025"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00004",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "Determining which procurement law regime applies? Generally, a procurement will be \"commenced\" on the date that the contract notice/advertisement is published. Contracts whose procurement was commenced before 24 February 2025 will continue to be regulated by the Public Contracts Regulations 2015 (or where relevant by the equivalent Utilities/Defence/Concessions regulations). Read more",
      "ordinal": 4,
      "heading_path": [
        "Procurements started before 24 February 2025"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00005",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "Generally, a procurement will be \"commenced\" on the date that the contract notice/advertisement is published.",
      "ordinal": 5,
      "heading_path": [
        "Procurements started before 24 February 2025"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00006",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "Contracts whose procurement was commenced before 24 February 2025 will continue to be regulated by the Public Contracts Regulations 2015 (or where relevant by the equivalent Utilities/Defence/Concessions regulations).",
      "ordinal": 6,
      "heading_path": [
        "Procurements started before 24 February 2025"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00007",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "Timescale trackers The contract award procedures under the Public Contracts Regulations 2015 and Utilities Contracts Regulations 2016 involve complex minimum timescales and potential reductions, making them confusing. Non-central government contracting authorities and utilities enjoy a certain amount of flexibility around the setting of timescales, subject to agreement with and safeguards for bidders. View trackers",
      "ordinal": 7,
      "heading_path": [
        "Procurements started before 24 February 2025"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00008",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "The contract award procedures under the Public Contracts Regulations 2015 and Utilities Contracts Regulations 2016 involve complex minimum timescales and potential reductions, making them confusing.",
      "ordinal": 8,
      "heading_path": [
        "Procurements started before 24 February 2025"
      ],
